1
00:00:07,180 --> 00:00:11,797
In order to retrieve this safe from
Suori's mansion, a party has been formed.

2
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:12,710
Afterwards,

3
00:00:12,793 --> 00:00:15,717
I'll be able to turn into a giant vending
machine and plug the hole in the wall.

4
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:18,177
There are seven of us,
including me and Lammis.

5
00:00:18,260 --> 00:00:23,057
Between all the rubble along our path, and
trying to avoid any unnecessary combat,

6
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:25,199
the route's been kinda complicated.

7
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:30,726
Based on the map, we should be
close once we get through there.

8
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:36,620
We finally made it to a section
of town, I know. Indeed.

9
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:39,646
If we follow this path,
we'll see the mansion.

10
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:49,520
My mansion's in ruins!

11
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:55,860
Before we came, I thought
I was prepared to see this.

12
00:00:57,840 --> 00:01:02,180
Seeing such a sad look on Suori's
face, I can't even find the words.

13
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:13,065
It was the first time I've ever seen her
ball like any known child her age would.

14
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:25,604
On the outside, I'm just a big metal box,
but inside, I've still got a human soul.

15
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:26,877
In this new world of wonders,

16
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:29,917
I travel to and fro on the back
of my super strong partner,

17
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:30,830
Lamas.

18
00:01:30,913 --> 00:01:32,880
The name's Boxo. Hello there.

19
00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:34,860
That means yes, by the way.

20
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:51,580
I'm not happy with my mood.

21
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:54,940
I'm not happy with my mood.

22
00:01:59,060 --> 00:02:01,077
If I get something like
that, I'll be right back.

23
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:03,278
I love it, but I will be right back.

24
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:06,137
I love it,

25
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:11,237
but I'll be right back.

26
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:53,680
I apologize for losing
my composure like that.

27
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:55,566
I'm feeling a lot better now.

28
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,350
Sorry.

29
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,944
The safe should be underground.

30
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:01,709
Watch your step, everyone.

31
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:02,980
All this art.

32
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:04,100
How awful.

33
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:06,300
To be honest, I expected as much.

34
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:09,217
The decorations seem
extravagant at first glance,

35
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:12,097
but they're actually more
affordable than you'd think.

36
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:13,062
Thank goodness.

37
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:15,673
Looks like she's back to her usual self.

38
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:19,040
Here, this way.

39
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:22,340
Whoa, there's a hidden basement down here?

40
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:25,560
This is it.

41
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:39,740
I knew she was rich, but
this is on another level!

42
00:03:40,260 --> 00:03:42,340
Look how much they managed to save!

43
00:03:42,660 --> 00:03:43,640
It's her home.

44
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:45,055
Why is she surprised?

45
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:47,573
Is this your first time down here, miss?

46
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:48,977
I see.

47
00:03:49,060 --> 00:03:51,857
Suori's never actually seen what's
in the basement safe before.

48
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:52,920
Remind me again.

49
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:56,240
You're unable to accept
gold bars, right, Boxo? Yes.

50
00:03:56,780 --> 00:03:59,877
In that case, I'll loan you
all the gold coins we have.

51
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:00,790
Thank yous.

52
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:05,300
Of course, you're most welcome, dear Boxo.

53
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:09,127
I'm happy to hear you finally
learned to say my name properly.

54
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:10,380
Wait a sec.

55
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:13,031
You can say my name, too, can't you, Boxo?

56
00:04:13,260 --> 00:04:14,090
Yes.

57
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:15,299
I want to hear it.

58
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:16,880
Lammis.

59
00:04:17,020 --> 00:04:18,197
You guys heard that, right?

60
00:04:18,280 --> 00:04:19,515
He said it correctly.

61
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:21,857
Sorry, it's still not perfect.

62
00:04:21,940 --> 00:04:23,822
If only I could say the me part.

63
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:27,577
If you really listen, he's saying
my name more clearly than yours.

64
00:04:27,660 --> 00:04:29,057
Well, I asked him to call me that.

65
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:30,787
It's like a secret nickname.

66
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:34,293
I had forgotten that these
two don't get along very well.

67
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:37,204
Suori was pretty pushy
when she tried to buy me.

68
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:39,477
Please, miss, we're short on time.

69
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:41,657
We should get back to the association.

70
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:42,880
Yes, yes, I know.

71
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:54,780
Let me remind you that this is just alone.

72
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:56,617
As soon as things settle down,

73
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:59,317
I intend to build the Hunters
Association accordingly.

74
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:01,957
She's probably trying to
hide her embarrassment.

75
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:04,717
They say adversity reveals
a person's character.

76
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:07,918
And it's clear that Suori
is a truly charming person.

77
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:12,800
They put in 110 gold coins, so
my points increased by 110,000.

78
00:05:13,340 --> 00:05:15,928
That should make the
next step a lot easier.

79
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:23,420
Hey, we're back!

80
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:28,220
Can you please give me a comb on Poxel?

81
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:29,600
No, me too!

82
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:30,900
He's finally back!

83
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:34,237
It looks like the heat's
starting to get to them.

84
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:35,400
Give me some ice.

85
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:37,469
Everybody, just calm down!

86
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:42,041
I'll give out ice cream and whatever
else you need, so form a line!

87
00:05:48,960 --> 00:05:50,960
Thankfully that's been dealt with.

88
00:05:51,060 --> 00:05:53,337
But this heat is getting worse by the day.

89
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:56,377
The residents won't be able to
tolerate this for much longer.

90
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:59,754
We've got to improve this
situation as soon as possible.

91
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:03,737
Let's start the meeting with a
discussion on how to repair the wall.

92
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:04,938
First things first,

93
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:09,137
with all the money that you've earned,
could you change into your giant form, Boxo?

94
00:06:09,220 --> 00:06:12,020
I could happen for a brief to happen.

95
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:14,536
How many hours could you maintain it?

96
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:17,260
One bottle.

97
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:21,137
In other words, you can hold
it for a single hour, correct?

98
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:22,050
Win!

99
00:06:22,133 --> 00:06:22,980
I see.

100
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:25,777
I'm considering ordering
an attack on the enemy

101
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:28,197
forces once they pull
back for the evening.

102
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:32,020
That said, if anyone has any
objections, feel free to speak up.

103
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:36,240
Director, I actually have an idea.

104
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,100
By all means, do tell.

105
00:06:39,020 --> 00:06:40,677
To boost our chance of success,

106
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:43,537
we'll wait for the enemy
to withdraw and sneak into

107
00:06:43,620 --> 00:06:46,738
a position near the hole
under the cover of darkness.

108
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:50,357
Then, we'll move on to
the next part of the plan.

109
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:53,817
Once the monsters launch their
assault on the Hunters Association,

110
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:56,417
they'll bring as much of
their army as they can muster?

111
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:57,997
leaving the hole unguarded.

112
00:06:58,080 --> 00:07:00,551
We'll use that to hit them where it hurts.

113
00:07:01,200 --> 00:07:04,057
This is probably our best
chance to fix the wall.

114
00:07:04,140 --> 00:07:06,420
That said, there's one problem.

115
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:10,877
If we go with your plan, our defenders
will be put in considerable danger.

116
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:11,790
I know.

117
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:16,009
I suppose that's a risk
we'll have to take.

118
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:20,760
You must steal yourselves.

119
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:23,437
This will likely be a
life-or-death struggle.

120
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:27,957
The combatants chosen to be part of the
Wall Repair Mission Task Force are Mishuel,

121
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:28,870
Shirley,

122
00:07:28,953 --> 00:07:30,760
the Band of Gluttons, and Umatei.

123
00:07:31,300 --> 00:07:32,637
Shimelai, three Earth Mages,

124
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:35,637
and I were the work detail
responsible for fixing the wall.

125
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:38,177
Voxo's role in the mission
is especially important.

126
00:07:38,260 --> 00:07:39,201
I wish you luck.

127
00:07:40,580 --> 00:07:42,857
This is a lot of
responsibility to place on

128
00:07:42,940 --> 00:07:45,117
a vending machine's
non-existent shoulders.

129
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:48,957
Though nowadays, vending machines are
expected to work during disasters.

130
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,981
That means I can't let them down.

131
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:52,180
Karios Gorth,

132
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:56,457
in the unlikely event we don't return from
our mission, I want you to hold the spot.

133
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:59,017
Thanks to the provisions
Boxo gave us last night,

134
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:02,377
you've got enough food to easily
last you at least a month.

135
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:06,477
Once other strata deal with their
issues, they'll send over reinforcements.

136
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:07,390
Stay strong.

137
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:09,624
That's what Director Bear said.

138
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:14,741
But everyone understood the likelihood of
help coming from the other strata was low.

139
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:27,317
There are so many of them, that this range
will end up croaked if they notice us.

140
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:28,280
Seems so.

141
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:32,957
We could easily kick their tails, but we
should wait for an opening to slip by.

142
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:33,870
He's right.

143
00:08:34,160 --> 00:08:37,689
We have to wait, and have faith
in those at the association.

144
00:08:38,700 --> 00:08:40,140
I'm a little worried.

145
00:08:40,380 --> 00:08:43,420
I hope Hulemy and the others
are okay. Hello there!

146
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:46,797
You could have just said, yeah, you know.

147
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:48,297
I'm sure they'll be fine.

148
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:50,733
Our reliable gate guards are there, too.

149
00:08:58,200 --> 00:08:59,030
Right.

150
00:08:59,113 --> 00:09:00,413
Sounds like it's begun.

151
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:02,360
We should go now!

152
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:05,020
You mustn't be impatient.

153
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:07,460
I understand how you feel right now.

154
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:09,477
But we need to wait a little more.

155
00:09:09,560 --> 00:09:10,660
But we...

156
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:28,017
The voluptuous figure
is as strong as ever.

157
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:31,837
Director please I'd rather you not
bring up such an embarrassing name.

158
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:34,917
Based on what director bear said
it sounds like miss shirley used

159
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:39,397
to be a hunter in the past with
her skills I believe it are you

160
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:42,877
ready it's time for you to enter
the hole from above and block it

161
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:45,317
off we're counting on you you the

162
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:50,697
act boxo I had a feeling that she

163
00:09:50,780 --> 00:09:56,737
wouldn't be happy about me going
in alone good luck in there I

164
00:09:56,820 --> 00:10:00,437
wasn't expecting that so those
sounds just came out I was totally

165
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:03,877
ready for her to lecture me or try
to stop me from going grandma I

166
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:07,037
used to say people don't like young
ladies who are too controlling?

167
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:10,897
so I've decided to have faith in you
and let you do what you think is right.

168
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:14,156
But that means you have to
come back in working order.

169
00:10:14,460 --> 00:10:16,340
Looks like Lamas is growing up.

170
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:19,132
I feel pumped knowing she believes in me.

171
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:21,100
Eat it to me.

172
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:25,780
Just proud, Boxo. Hello there.

173
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:37,940
I'd love to wave back but I don't have
any arms so this will have to do for now.

174
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:44,677
All right I'll be back

175
00:10:52,300 --> 00:10:56,418
There are countless monsters gathering
together from outside the wall.

176
00:10:56,580 --> 00:10:58,140
They're marching in sync.

177
00:10:58,420 --> 00:11:01,067
It's surprising how
coordinated they all are.

178
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:03,320
Anyway, I don't have time to waste.

179
00:11:05,560 --> 00:11:07,120
Drop point confirmed.

180
00:11:07,460 --> 00:11:08,380
Position check.

181
00:11:08,740 --> 00:11:09,660
Angle check.

182
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:11,060
Altitude check.

183
00:11:11,540 --> 00:11:12,560
Initiating drop.

184
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:14,100
Now form change.

185
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:15,810
Kaboom!

186
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:18,500
Huh? Huh?

187
00:11:18,660 --> 00:11:21,131
The frog fiends are making a break for it.

188
00:11:21,340 --> 00:11:22,360
Wait a sec.

189
00:11:22,540 --> 00:11:26,517
Could that impact have interrupted whatever
process that was keeping them in line?

190
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:29,517
If their chain of command is
broken, this is our chance.

191
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:32,953
Time to use the newest function
I've added to my arsenal.

192
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:36,137
The vending machine installation
mount concrete slab.

193
00:11:36,220 --> 00:11:39,097
Under normal circumstances, you'd
fix a vending machine in place?

194
00:11:39,180 --> 00:11:41,651
by embedding anchors into a concrete slab.

195
00:11:41,740 --> 00:11:45,037
But we'll skip that part for now
and activate the new function again.

196
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:47,337
In order to support such a large object,

197
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:49,837
These concrete slabs are
each over a meter thick.

198
00:11:49,920 --> 00:11:52,332
The hole is only about 10 meters in size,

199
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:55,067
so I just need to use
this function 10 times.

200
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:57,600
And like that, the pile is done.

201
00:11:58,320 --> 00:11:59,860
Great! It worked!

202
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:04,580
Now, go, fight!

203
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:09,140
You're not getting past me!

204
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:11,759
Director Bear's going all out, huh?

205
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,797
But the power from this big
frame and those sharp claws...

206
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:18,115
I kind of feel bad for any
monsters who get in his way.

207
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:24,437
Hey, Slowpoke, come and catch us!

208
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:25,696
If you can, that is!

209
00:12:28,140 --> 00:12:30,199
Oh, that must be the roar blessing!

210
00:12:36,340 --> 00:12:39,752
All right, I'd say it's about
our turn now, right, Gramps?

211
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:41,762
You've got it, Gramps, let's go!

212
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:58,470
Nice.

213
00:12:58,553 --> 00:13:00,277
Everything's going according to plan.

214
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:03,419
But it feels like the
monsters are organizing again.

215
00:13:03,620 --> 00:13:05,757
It would make sense if one
of the Netherlord's buddies

216
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:09,075
was hiding somewhere nearby
and issuing orders to them.

217
00:13:09,780 --> 00:13:10,610
Typically,

218
00:13:10,693 --> 00:13:14,797
a commander would position themselves so
they're safe distance from the front lines.

219
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:15,710
That said,

220
00:13:15,793 --> 00:13:17,397
they'd still need to have a
good view of the battlefield

221
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:19,897
and usually have guards
stationed around them.

222
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:22,804
Though, of course, nobody's
ever that formulaic.

223
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:24,190
Huh?

224
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:25,820
There he is, right there.

225
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:28,777
He's wearing a black robe just how the

226
00:13:28,860 --> 00:13:30,897
Netherlord and the King
of Souls were dressed.

227
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:32,940
Yeah, not suspicious at all.

228
00:13:33,820 --> 00:13:34,650
Right-o!

229
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:40,417
I could just crush him as
an ice vending machine,

230
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:42,559
but if he works for the Netherlord,

231
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:44,229
we should interrogate him.

232
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:46,070
Okay.

233
00:13:46,153 --> 00:13:47,525
I'll use my normal form, then.

234
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:51,880
What's going on?

235
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:53,430
Huh?

236
00:13:53,513 --> 00:13:54,380
The commander is a human?

237
00:13:54,900 --> 00:13:57,177
I kind of assumed that he'd be a skeleton.

238
00:13:57,260 --> 00:13:59,257
But I guess it's not that strange for some

239
00:13:59,340 --> 00:14:02,105
humans to decide to serve
under the Netherlord.

240
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:04,339
Where did this blue wall come from?

241
00:14:04,460 --> 00:14:05,290
You there!

242
00:14:05,373 --> 00:14:06,611
Prince of Wallet Freeman!

243
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:13,420
I can withstand this abuse for a
while, but my points aren't infinite.

244
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:15,500
Time to end this!

245
00:14:18,340 --> 00:14:21,105
Wait, where the heck is
that voice coming from?

246
00:14:22,700 --> 00:14:25,377
Text-to-speak voice isn't
all that intimidating.

247
00:14:25,460 --> 00:14:27,337
But getting through to
him is what matters.

248
00:14:27,420 --> 00:14:28,538
Stop, please, stop!

249
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:30,640
Spare my life, I'm begging you!

250
00:14:33,700 --> 00:14:35,837
I can't understand what you're saying!

251
00:14:35,920 --> 00:14:37,040
Please, release me!

252
00:14:37,260 --> 00:14:39,220
Yep, I knew he'd play innocent.

253
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:43,486
